{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion: The model consistently overestimates prices following sharp spikes (e.g., the 76+ EUR peak), failing to anticipate the rapid drop back to the 68-72 EUR range. Apply a downward correction of 3-5 EUR to forecasts 10-20 days out after any price exceeds 75 EUR.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: The model ignores negative sentiment signals (value -1.00) and positive spikes (value 1.00), treating them as neutral. When sentiment history shows a -1.00, reduce the 30-day forecast by 2-3 EUR to account for the subsequent price dip.",
    "Reduce forecast slope: The model exhibits a persistent upward drift (positive slope) regardless of the actual sideways or downward trend in the true data. Flatten the forecast curve by removing the artificial daily increase of ~0.03-0.05 EUR.",
    "Cap long-term horizon: Forecasts beyond day 15 systematically overshoot the true mean (approx. 71 EUR). Cap all long-term predictions at the historical mean of 71.50 EUR rather than allowing them to drift higher.",
    "Invert spike reaction: When the model forecasts a continuation of a high-price trend, the true outcome typically reverses. If the forecast is above 74 EUR, assume a high probability of a correction to the 70-72 EUR band within the next 5-7 days."
  ]
}
